solution:
The vertices of the shaded quadrilateral are  
\((1,0),\;(3,5),\;(5,0),\;(3,2)\).

Using the shoelace formula:

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Sum}_1 &= 1\cdot5 + 3\cdot0 + 5\cdot2 + 3\cdot0 = 15,\\
\text{Sum}_2 &= 0\cdot3 + 5\cdot5 + 0\cdot3 + 2\cdot1 = 27,\\
\text{Area} &= \frac{|\,\text{Sum}_1-\text{Sum}_2\,|}{2}
            = \frac{|15-27|}{2}
            = \frac{12}{2}
            = 6.
\end{aligned}
\]

Thus the area of the shaded figure is \(6\) square units.

